---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import { SITE } from '../lib/site.mjs';
---

<Base
  title="CLI — Specimen"
  description="Fetch a verified DESIGN.md into your repository from the command line."
>
  <div class="prose">
    <h1 style="margin-top:2rem;">The CLI</h1>
    <p>
      Fetches a verified DESIGN.md into your repository and prints the prompt to
      hand your agent. It validates the file before writing it, so a
      non-conformant file never reaches your working directory.
    </p>

    <h2>Install</h2>
    <p>
      <strong>Not published to npm yet.</strong> The scoped package name is
      reserved but nothing has been released, so <code>npx</code> will not find
      it. Until it ships, run it from a clone:
    </p>
    <pre><code>git clone https://github.com/MrPiThon/usespecimen
cd usespecimen
npm install</code></pre>
    <p>
      Requires Node 24. The commands below need no browser — only
      <code>extract</code> does, and that is for building the registry rather
      than consuming it.
    </p>

    <h2>Commands</h2>

    <h3>list</h3>
    <p>Show what the registry carries, with each system's palette and the date it was verified.</p>
    <pre><code>npm run list</code></pre>

    <h3>add</h3>
    <p>
      Write one system's DESIGN.md into the current directory. Refuses to
      overwrite an existing file without <code>--force</code>, and refuses
      outright if the fetched file does not conform to the spec.
    </p>
    <pre><code>npm run add -- stripe
npm run add -- stripe --force</code></pre>

    <h3>Pointing at another registry</h3>
    <p>
      Both commands talk to <code>{SITE}</code> by default. <code>--registry</code>
      points them somewhere else — a local <code>npm run build && npx astro preview</code>,
      or your own deployment:
    </p>
    <pre><code>npm run list -- --registry http://localhost:4321</code></pre>

    <h2>Building the registry</h2>
    <p>
      The other half of the CLI is the extraction pipeline. It needs Chromium
      (<code>npx playwright install chromium</code>) and is only relevant if you
      are adding systems rather than consuming them.
    </p>
    <pre><code>npm run extract -- https://stripe.com
npm run cluster -- out/stripe/capture.json</code></pre>
    <p>
      <code>extract</code> captures three widths under both colour schemes and
      writes <code>out/&lt;slug&gt;/capture.json</code> plus a screenshot.
      <code>cluster</code> re-runs the deterministic half over a saved capture
      with no browser and no network, which is the loop for tuning the clusterer
      against fixtures.
    </p>

    <p style="margin-top:2rem;">
      Prefer to skip the terminal? <a href="/mcp">The MCP server</a> gives an
      agent the same access without one.
    </p>
  </div>
</Base>
